<p>Grade A (retail)            ~65-75% of total volume   Main money Grade B / cracked / liquid  ~25-30%                   Versova (regional breaker), low margin Spoilage / waste            ~1-5%                     Negative</p>
<p>Source: Calder [00:15:14].</p>
<h3>3. manure offtake - real revenue offset, often missed</h3>
<p>NZ layer-farm manure goes to Ravensdown and Ballance Agri-Nutrients - the two main NZ fertiliser co-ops - as a Class A organic input. Pricing typically NZ$15-25 per tonne depending on year, moisture, and stockpile age.</p>
<p>For Aurora:</p>
<p>Bird population     ~610k layer flock Manure throughput   ~18,000-22,000 tonnes / year Realized revenue    NZ$300,000-500,000 / year (NZ$280k peak Calder year cited as a comparable benchmark for a ~600k-bird operation the size of Aurora&#x27;s)</p>
<p>Belongs in T3 bottom-line opportunities section as a quantified revenue offset that often gets missed in shell-egg sell-side framing (per the Halberd analytical standards section 8: &quot;Bottom-line / cost- out levers are commonly under-weighted by analysts focused on top-line stories&quot;).</p>
<p>Source: Calder [00:12:22]; Calthorpe Part 7 [00:51:14] (Bucket 4 supplier exposure annex, 3 June, section 9).</p>
<h3>4. alternative-use optionality - realistic scenario set</h3>
